GIVEN `the appeal was made to the Appellate Division in accordance with section 29C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the appeal made to the Appellate Division in accordance with section 29C(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29D(5) the appeal may be transferred under section 29D(1) even though it was made in accordance with section 29C(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appeal was made to the Appellate Division in accordance with section 29C(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "even if it was made to the Appellate Division in accordance with section 29C(1)"

